# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/exact-end window (exact resume P0 on the production stack; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/exact-end and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-xe-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory, in the prefix gate's
# containers too (c2_prefix_gate.py reads every arm's log for the checkpoint lines and fails the arm without them); the keys are the same in every serving job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# XT (P0 BESIDE THE HOST KV TIER, SOFT; the production profile carries the 32 GiB tier and the preconverted checkpoints): the prefix gate's tier-returning plan
# (prefix_replay.scenario_tier_returning) on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-xe-audit, Swift: sessions built to about 56k, fresh-salt floods totalling
# the whole KV pool so that every cached block of the sessions leaves the device pool (spilled to host RAM), then each session's next turn as a cold/hit pair (the hit's
# blocks come back from the host and its checkpoint resumes ONE CHUNK HIGHER than the tier pack measured, the window rows carried with the checkpoint), one more turn on a
# restored session and the tier's own kill switch. Nothing in P0 touches the tier or the checkpoint's preconverted tensors (the carried rows are a separate attribute of the
# same checkpoint); this is the card read of that claim. READ: the plan PASS: every pair IDENTICAL, the restore and the spill on record, a carried admission on a restored
# session, every window audit exact=True, the tier counters at zero failures, no tier latch beyond the drilled kill switch; CHECKPOINT READ (the prefix gate checks every
# arm's container log, the smoke step passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the arm's
# result line says "checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a: read".. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. Duration (estimate): about 2 hours (an audited boot, the floods
# and the cold twins).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-xe-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-returning
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s4-xe-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=170
